# Golden files are byte-exact fixtures: the tests compare the encoder's output
# against them literally, so a line-ending conversion on checkout turns every
# golden test red on Windows with a diff that looks identical when printed,
# because the only difference is an invisible carriage return.
#
# eol=lf (rather than -text) keeps them checked out as LF on every platform
# while still letting git diff them as text when a golden legitimately changes.
*.golden text eol=lf

# Go source is LF by convention and gofmt assumes it.
*.go text eol=lf
